from pathlib import Path
import zipfile
root=Path('outputs/Mechanical_Design_App')
p=root/'README.md';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8')+'''\n\n## Version 0.7 — editable pilot revision export (Phase 4 of 7)\n\nExport proposed joint revision creates a ZIP with pi4_proposed.scad and revision.json using current draft selections/inputs. It changes only insert_pilot in the bundled clearance-v2 source. No baseline, project selection or database is changed by export. Source metadata includes pinned hardware snapshots, all check outcomes and unresolved limitations.\n\nThe narrow Pi4 adapter supports M3 x 0.5 joint hardware, stack 3.3 mm, pocket 8 mm, boss diameter 9 mm and pilot diameter 3–4.2 mm. Unsupported geometry changes or any failed dimensional check block export. Unknowns do not become passes: exports are marked PROPOSED — UNVALIDATED. This is an editable-source export, not an STL generator or automatic manufacturing validation.\n\nWith the supplied M3 inserts, the original 4.2 mm pilot fails the 4 mm supplier maximum. A 4 mm setting can be exported as a trial, not a confirmed installation diameter; exact fit still requires a coupon and complete insert dimensions. The pilot changes the faceplate boss bores, not the tray screw ears.\n\nValidation: twelve tests pass, including binary ZIP endpoint, metadata, draft persistence, failed-check blocking and exact baseline-to-proposal source comparison. JavaScript syntax passes. A 4 mm pilot proposal renders in OpenSCAD as a simple faceplate solid. That render does not establish insert suitability or full assembly clearance. Live browser export testing remains pending.\n\nThe 3D viewer continues showing v2 manufacturing meshes and linked hardware reference envelopes; it does not display the proposed pilot until a future mesh-regeneration step. Phase 4 remains in progress. Stop the server, replace app files including pi4_baseline.scad, keep data/, restart and refresh.\n''';p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
with zipfile.ZipFile('outputs/Mechanical_Design_App_Beta_0_7.zip','w',zipfile.ZIP_DEFLATED) as z:
 for p in root.iterdir():
  if p.is_file():z.write(p,Path(root.name)/p.name)
with zipfile.ZipFile('outputs/Mechanical_Design_App_Beta_0_7.zip') as z:assert z.testzip() is None
print('Beta 0.7 archive validated.')
